WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.816
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.116 --> 00:00:08.804
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:14.740
Unit five: Global Cuisine. Today you will talk about food wishes and experiences.

4
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.751
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.153
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:24.262
Fusion food.

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.805
Fusion food means food that mixes two or more cooking styles.

8
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:32.113
Kimchi tacos are fusion food.

9
00:00:32.717 --> 00:00:35.648
Your turn. Say: Fusion food.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.606
Fusion food.

11
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.746
Authentic dish.

12
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.481
Authentic dish means food made the traditional way.

13
00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:48.315
This is an authentic dish from Kampot.

14
00:00:48.917 --> 00:00:51.627
Your turn. Say: Authentic dish.

15
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:55.793
Authentic dish.

16
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.992
Regional specialty.

17
00:00:58.983 --> 00:01:02.411
Regional specialty means a food famous in one area.

18
00:01:03.017 --> 00:01:05.527
Kampot crab is a regional specialty.

19
00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:08.885
Your turn. Say: Regional specialty.

20
00:01:11.733 --> 00:01:13.373
Regional specialty.

21
00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:15.663
Culinary tradition.

22
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.764
Culinary tradition means the cooking customs of a place.

23
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.744
Italy has a rich culinary tradition.

24
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:26.281
Your turn. Say: Culinary tradition.

25
00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:30.460
Culinary tradition.

26
00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:32.450
Spice blend.

27
00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.076
Spice blend means a mix of spices.

28
00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:38.753
Kroeung is a Khmer spice blend.

29
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.118
Your turn. Say: Spice blend.

30
00:01:44.967 --> 00:01:46.455
Spice blend.

31
00:01:47.217 --> 00:01:48.369
Street food.

32
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:52.521
Street food means food sold at stalls on the street.

33
00:01:53.117 --> 00:01:55.604
Num banh chok is great street food.

34
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:59.113
Your turn. Say: Street food.

35
00:02:01.967 --> 00:02:03.084
Street food.

36
00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:04.967
Fine dining.

37
00:02:05.983 --> 00:02:09.434
Fine dining means eating at an expensive, elegant restaurant.

38
00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.595
We tried fine dining for Mum's birthday.

39
00:02:13.183 --> 00:02:15.940
Your turn. Say: Fine dining.

40
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.010
Fine dining.

41
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:21.914
Food culture.

42
00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:26.600
Food culture means the way a society eats and shares food.

43
00:02:27.183 --> 00:02:29.868
Sharing plates is part of Khmer food culture.

44
00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:33.414
Your turn. Say: Food culture.

45
00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:37.384
Food culture.

46
00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.453
Signature dish.

47
00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.226
Signature dish means the most famous dish of a chef or place.

48
00:02:44.817 --> 00:02:47.350
Fish amok is the restaurant's signature dish.

49
00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.939
Your turn. Say: Signature dish.

50
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.219
Signature dish.

51
00:02:55.983 --> 00:02:57.310
Flavor profile.

52
00:02:58.317 --> 00:03:01.210
Flavor profile means the mix of tastes in a food.

53
00:03:01.817 --> 00:03:05.430
Thai food has a sweet, sour and spicy flavor profile.

54
00:03:06.017 --> 00:03:09.110
Your turn. Say: Flavor profile.

55
00:03:11.967 --> 00:03:13.362
Flavor profile.

56
00:03:14.117 --> 00:03:15.338
Gastronomy.

57
00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:19.023
Gastronomy means the art and study of good food.

58
00:03:19.617 --> 00:03:22.313
Lyon in France is famous for gastronomy.

59
00:03:22.917 --> 00:03:26.173
Your turn. Say: Gastronomy.

60
00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.278
Gastronomy.

61
00:03:31.017 --> 00:03:31.832
Palate.

62
00:03:32.817 --> 00:03:34.932
Palate means your sense of taste.

63
00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:37.214
Travel broadens your palate.

64
00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.306
Your turn. Say: Palate.

65
00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:44.017
Palate.

66
00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:48.380
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:49.217 --> 00:03:52.575
Visal, which dish from another culture would you like to try?

68
00:03:53.683 --> 00:03:57.566
I would like to try authentic Japanese ramen. I have never tried it.

69
00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:00.719
Have you ever tried fusion food?

70
00:04:01.817 --> 00:04:08.274
No, I have never tried fusion food, but I would like to try kimchi tacos!

71
00:04:09.383 --> 00:04:11.650
What would you recommend from Khmer cuisine?

72
00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:18.932
Fish amok. Its spice blend, kroeung, gives it a unique flavor profile.

73
00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:22.519
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:23.383 --> 00:04:26.915
Grammar focus: would like to try and have never tried.

75
00:04:27.215 --> 00:04:28.414
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:29.117 --> 00:04:30.849
I would like to try this dish.

77
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.657
I have never tried fusion food.

78
00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:38.070
She would like to visit Italy, but she has never eaten real pizza.

79
00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:45.227
Use 'would like to' + base verb for a wish. Use 'have never' + past participle for no experience.

80
00:04:45.983 --> 00:04:49.762
Be careful! Don't say: I have never try fusion food.

81
00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:54.431
Say: I have never tried fusion food.

82
00:04:54.731 --> 00:04:57.114
After 'have never', use the past participle.

83
00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.715
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.989
A World of Flavours.

85
00:05:03.289 --> 00:05:06.786
Fusion food combines culinary traditions from different regions.

86
00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:11.204
Each country has a signature dish and a unique spice blend.

87
00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.722
I have never tried authentic Indian curry.

88
00:05:15.733 --> 00:05:19.045
I would like to try it because its flavor profile is rich.

89
00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:23.531
Exploring street food and fine dining broadens your palate.

90
00:05:24.633 --> 00:05:28.821
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:29.683 --> 00:05:31.764
I have never blank fusion food.

92
00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:35.404
A, tried. B, try. C, trying.

93
00:05:38.967 --> 00:05:40.850
The answer is A: tried.

94
00:05:42.017 --> 00:05:44.539
Food sold at stalls on the street is blank.

95
00:05:44.839 --> 00:05:49.107
A, street food. B, fine dining. C, gastronomy.

96
00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.991
The answer is A: street food.

97
00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:58.033
Your sense of taste is your blank.

98
00:05:58.333 --> 00:06:01.720
A, palate. B, palette. C, flavor.

99
00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:07.336
The answer is A: palate.

100
00:06:08.533 --> 00:06:11.778
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:12.617 --> 00:06:15.580
Describe a dish from another culture you would like to try.

102
00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:25.872
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:26.172 --> 00:06:35.117
I would like to try Korean bibimbap. I have never tried it, but I love rice and vegetables, so I think I would enjoy it.

104
00:06:35.417 --> 00:06:37.184
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:38.083 --> 00:06:43.301
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and would like to try and have never tried.

106
00:06:43.601 --> 00:06:49.354
Today's value is cultural appreciation. Enjoy and respect the music and art of every culture.

107
00:06:49.654 --> 00:06:52.062
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

108
00:06:52.362 --> 00:06:56.199
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

